    {
      "id": "0021:A1",
      "kind": "A",
      "key": "1",
      "label": "The respond gateway's `TextLiner` seam prints a multi-line `Data` string verbatim on stdout in text mode, with no decoration, reordering, or trailing content beyond one final newline — including under provoked notes/warnings, which stay on stderr.",
      "derived": false,
      "hash": "d360b761",
      "section": "0021:§critical-assumptions",
      "line_start": 114,
      "line_end": 130,
      "bytes": 964,
      "fields": [
        {
          "label": "Status",
          "canonical": "Status",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "Verified",
          "section": "0021:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0021:A1",
          "line_start": 118,
          "line_end": 118,
          "status": {
            "value": "Verified",
            "tier": "canonical",
            "raw": "Verified"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": "Method",
          "canonical": "Method",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "Spike",
          "section": "0021:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0021:A1",
          "line_start": 119,
          "line_end": 119,
          "method": {
            "members": [
              "Spike"
            ],
            "raw": "Spike"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": "Evidence",
          "canonical": "Evidence",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "`internal/cli/respond/respond.go::TextLiner` exists and `OK` prints it via `Fprintln`; the spike byte-compared `stdout == document + \"\\n\"` for a multi-kilobyte multi-line payload with advisories provoked (premortem P-5/P-15) — byte-identical in both arms, notes/warnings confined to stderr (`evidence/spikes/a1-textliner.md`). Normative fixture F1: text-mode stdout is exactly `document + \"\\n\"`, stderr empty absent advisories.",
          "section": "0021:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0021:A1",
          "line_start": 120,
          "line_end": 127
        },
        {
          "label": "If wrong",
          "canonical": "If wrong",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "the bare-document text mode gains stray bytes, CI diffs of the export break, and C5 needs a gateway extension instead of a ride on the existing seam.",
          "section": "0021:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0021:A1",
          "line_start": 128,
          "line_end": 130
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0021:A2",
      "kind": "A",
      "key": "2",
      "label": "The reachable node set and its successor edges are a deterministic function of the model value, and the edge list is recoverable after the fixpoint by re-running `successorsOf` over the final nodes with subsumption mapping (`indexOf`), yielding EXACTLY the edges the traversal itself took — over-approximation by merged re-run is the premortem's central defect (P-1), so equality, not plausibility, is the bar.",
      "derived": false,
      "hash": "30b7bcc9",
      "section": "0021:§critical-assumptions",
      "line_start": 131,
      "line_end": 166,
      "bytes": 2269,
      "fields": [
        {
          "label": "Status",
          "canonical": "Status",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "Verified — with a recorded coupling: holds because `indexOf` uses `subsumes`, which makes `reach()`'s in-place widening arm unreachable (exhaustive lemma + zero-event audit, `evidence/spikes/a2-edge-recovery.md`)",
          "section": "0021:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0021:A2",
          "line_start": 138,
          "line_end": 141,
          "status": {
            "value": "Verified",
            "qualifier": "with a recorded coupling: holds because indexOf uses subsumes, which makes reach()'s in-place widening arm unreachable (exhaustive lemma + zero-event audit, evidence/spikes/a2-edge-recovery.md)",
            "tier": "canonical",
            "raw": "Verified — with a recorded coupling: holds because `indexOf` uses `subsumes`, which makes `reach()`'s in-place widening arm unreachable (exhaustive lemma + zero-event audit, `evidence/spikes/a2-edge-recovery.md`)"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": "Method",
          "canonical": "Method",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "Spike",
          "section": "0021:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0021:A2",
          "line_start": 142,
          "line_end": 142,
          "method": {
            "members": [
              "Spike"
            ],
            "raw": "Spike"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": "Evidence",
          "canonical": "Evidence",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "`internal/graphlint/reach.go::reach` iterates slices, not maps, and `successorsOf` appends in first-seen row order. The spike showed (a) repeated runs byte-identical including under `GODEBUG=randmapiter=1`, and (b) a DIFFERENTIAL test — an observer recording edges during the traversal vs the post-hoc recovery — giving EXACT multiset equality over synthetic fixtures A–I and all 36 authored models (`EQUAL=36, NOT-EQUAL=0`), with a negative control (injected phantom/dropped edge) and a positive control (a weakened `indexOf` made the arm live and diverge by 2 edges), so the harness detects divergence rather than defaulting green. The coupling: `subsumes` requires an identical key set plus value coverage, so `joinNodes(nodes[j], next)` is always key-equal to `nodes[j]` and the `merged.key() == nodes[j].key()` guard fires first (`a2-edge-recovery.md:59-64`). The property is pinned in CODE, not restated here — kata `yybx` ships the behaviour regression test and the stale-comment fix in isolation from this RDR; once landed, that test is the property's home. Graded `constraint` (answer fixed by shipped code, `5e57b79`); it does not gate the lock.",
          "section": "0021:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0021:A2",
          "line_start": 143,
          "line_end": 161
        },
        {
          "label": "If wrong",
          "canonical": "If wrong",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "the named fallback is the in-traversal edge observer (record edges as `reach` takes them); that arm is admissible because C4's neutrality oracle — lint byte-identical with and without the export code — is stated mechanism-independently and the MVV asserts it either way (P-14).",
          "section": "0021:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0021:A2",
          "line_start": 162,
          "line_end": 166
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0021:A3",
      "kind": "A",
      "key": "3",
      "label": "The normalized model value carries everything the document needs — declarations with finite domains (via `guard.AssignmentCount`), `[initial]`, `terminal`, normalized rows with blocked atoms, and `guard.Groups` — with no re-parse of the authored TOML.",
      "derived": false,
      "hash": "00f01b6a",
      "section": "0021:§critical-assumptions",
      "line_start": 167,
      "line_end": 192,
      "bytes": 1629,
      "fields": [
        {
          "label": "Status",
          "canonical": "Status",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "Verified (declarations, tags, initial, terminal, rows, groups, nodes); the edge relation is derived in the export path as a pure function of the model value — see A2",
          "section": "0021:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0021:A3",
          "line_start": 172,
          "line_end": 174,
          "status": {
            "value": "Verified",
            "qualifier": "(declarations, tags, initial, terminal, rows, groups, nodes); the edge relation is derived in the export path as a pure function of the model value — see A2",
            "tier": "canonical",
            "raw": "Verified (declarations, tags, initial, terminal, rows, groups, nodes); the edge relation is derived in the export path as a pure function of the model value — see A2"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": "Method",
          "canonical": "Method",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "Source Search",
          "section": "0021:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0021:A3",
          "line_start": 175,
          "line_end": 175,
          "method": {
            "members": [
              "Source Search"
            ],
            "raw": "Source Search"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": "Evidence",
          "canonical": "Evidence",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "`internal/table/model.go` field walk against the C2 field list (`Model.ID`/`Class`/`Tags`/`Initial`/`Terminal`/`Rows`), `internal/guard/declaration.go::AssignmentCount` for finite domains, `internal/guard/product.go::Groups` for the partition, and `internal/graphlint/reach.go::Reach` for nodes — every one a pure function of the model value with no TOML re-parse (`evidence/research/a3-a4.md`). The edge relation is NOT carried by the model value: `reach()` computes nodes only and `successorsOf` reads `row.RuleID` but discards it, so no edge carrier exists today. It is constructible with no re-parse (the rule id is on `table.Row.RuleID`) and is recovered in the export path per A2. This narrows the pre-edit wording (\"carries everything the document needs\"), which overstated the model value's coverage; narrowed at Resolve 2026-09-12. C2 is unchanged — it predicates *carries* of the document, which still carries edges.",
          "section": "0021:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0021:A3",
          "line_start": 176,
          "line_end": 190
        },
        {
          "label": "If wrong",
          "canonical": "If wrong",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "the schema shrinks, or a loader extension becomes a prerequisite and the blast radius grows past this RDR.",
          "section": "0021:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0021:A3",
          "line_start": 191,
          "line_end": 192
        }
      ]
    },
    {
